// Jest Snapshot v1, https://jestjs.io/docs/snapshot-testing

exports[`CLI help interface for 'idm remote-proxy teardown' should be expected english 1`] = `
"Usage: frodo idm remote-proxy teardown [options] [host] [realm] [username] [password]

[Cloud-only] Take down an IDM remote proxy and what frodo idm remote-proxy setup
created for it, in the reverse order.

It cuts the access first: on the receiving tenant it deletes the static user
mapping, which stops the proxy at once, and then the OAuth2 client. Deleting
only the client would leave a proxy that already holds a token working until the
token expires. Then, on this tenant, it deletes the remote proxy, the ESV
variable and the ESV secret. IDM refuses to delete the variable for about a
minute after the proxy is gone, so that delete is retried. --keep-client leaves
the receiving tenant alone, which also leaves the access in place, and a client
that another remote proxy still uses is kept. The receiving tenant is found from
the host name the proxy's ESV variable holds, or given with --target.

It lists what it will delete and asks for confirmation. It is safe to run again:
what is already gone is skipped.

Arguments:
  host                       AM base URL, e.g.: https://cdk.iam.example.com/am.
                             To use a connection profile, just specify a unique
                             substring or alias.
  realm                      Realm. Specify realm as '/' for the root realm or
                             'realm' or '/parent/child' otherwise. (default:
                             "alpha" for Identity Cloud tenants, "/" otherwise.)
  username                   Username to login with. Must be an admin user with
                             appropriate rights to manage authentication
                             journeys/trees. If given without a password, and it
                             matches the username already stored in the
                             connection profile for the target host, frodo uses
                             that profile's stored password instead of requiring
                             it on the command line.
  password                   Password.

Deployment: Cloud-only

Options:
  --dry-run                  Show what would be deleted on which tenant and
                             change nothing.
  -i, --proxy-id <proxy-id>  Remote proxy name. (pick from remote proxy)
                             (prompts if missing)
  --keep-client              Leave the receiving tenant alone: its OAuth2 client
                             and static user mapping stay.
  --target <host url>        Host URL of the receiving tenant, if it cannot be
                             found from the proxy. The URL must resolve to an
                             existing connection profile. (pick from connection
                             profile)
  --timeout <seconds>        How long to keep retrying the delete of the ESV
                             secret and variable. (default: 300 secs (5 mins))
  -y, --yes                  Do not ask for confirmation before deleting.
  -h, --help                 Help
  -hh, --help-more           Help with all options.
  -hhh, --help-all           Help with all options, environment variables, and
                             usage examples.
"
`;
